IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-members`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-inspection`

-- coa3-tests-inspection.l4: tests for coa3-part8-inspection.l4 (ss 114 to 128ZA).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the code was run.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered.

-- ---- s 114(1): arguments (place) (a restriction under s 120A applies) ----
#ASSERT `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` `s 114(1)(a) at its registered office` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` `s 114(1)(b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` `s 114(1) at another place` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` `s 114(1)(a) at its registered office` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` `s 114(1) at another place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- s 114(2) ----
#ASSERT `s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register is kept available and of any change in that place` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register is kept available and of any change in that place` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register is kept available and of any change in that place` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place (duty)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 114(2) the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the register is kept` AT 3
-- ---- s 114(3): arguments (in existence on the relevant date) (at all times since it came into existence at the registered office) (at all times since the relevant date at the registered office) ----
#ASSERT `s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ---- s 114(4): "(a) 1st July 1948 in the case of a company registered in Great Britain, and (b) 1st April 1961 in the case of a company registered in Northern Ireland" ----
#ASSERT `s 114(4) the relevant date for the purposes of s 114(3)` `England and Wales` EQUALS Date 1 7 1948
#ASSERT `s 114(4) the relevant date for the purposes of s 114(3)` Scotland EQUALS Date 1 7 1948
#ASSERT `s 114(4) the relevant date for the purposes of s 114(3)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS Date 1 4 1961
-- ---- s 114(5): "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)": arguments (days of default) (person) (s 1121) ----
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 13 Company (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 0 Director (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 14 Company NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 15 Director (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 14 Director (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 14 `Company secretary` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` 30 Member (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(6) the penalty for an offence under s 114` EQUALS (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 115(1): "Every company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names ... unless the register ... constitutes in itself an index": arguments (members) (register is itself an index) ----
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` 50 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` 51 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` 51 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` 10 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 115(2): "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register": 1 March 2023 gives 15 March 2023
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS Date 15 3 2023
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` (Date 25 12 2023) EQUALS Date 8 1 2024
-- arguments: (answer of s 115(1)) (register altered on) (index altered on)
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 15 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 16 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 28 2 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` NOTHING (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the index meets the requirement of a sufficient indication for each member` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the index meets the requirement of a sufficient indication for each member` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(4) the index must at all times be kept available for inspection at the same place as the register, subject to s 115(4A)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(4) the index must at all times be kept available for inspection at the same place as the register, subject to s 115(4A)` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(5) the person commits an offence` FALSE Company (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(5) the person commits an offence` TRUE Company NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(5) the person commits an offence` TRUE Director (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(5) the person commits an offence` TRUE Director (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(5) the person commits an offence` TRUE Member (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(6) the penalty for an offence under s 115` EQUALS (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 116(1)(a): arguments (member) (restriction) ----
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(a) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection without charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(a) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection without charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(a) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection without charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 116(1)(b): arguments (member) (the prescribed fee is paid) (restriction)
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 116(2): arguments (fee paid) (restriction)
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the person may require a copy of the register of members or of any part of it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the person may require a copy of the register of members or of any part of it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the person may require a copy of the register of members or of any part of it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the person must make a request to the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the person must make a request to the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 116(4): the request. Fields in order: individual; name and address; purpose; says whether disclosed; will be disclosed; the other person is an individual; the other's name and address; the other's purpose ----
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 117 ----
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company must within five working days either comply with the request or apply to the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company must within five working days either comply with the request or apply to the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "within five working days": the count of working days after receipt
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty as a regulative rule (day 0 = receipt of the request, counted in working days): complying on day 5 or applying to the court on day 3 fulfils it; neither by day 6 breaches it
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company must within five working days comply with the request or apply to the court (duty)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request` AT 5
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company must within five working days comply with the request or apply to the court (duty)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court` AT 3
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company must within five working days comply with the request or apply to the court (duty)` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 6)
#ASSERT `s 117(2) the company must notify the person making the request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(2) the company must notify the person making the request` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 117(3)(a): arguments (an application is made) (the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose)
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 117(3)(b): arguments (application) (satisfied) (the person who made the request is a party): "even if he is not a party to the application"
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant or a power and the "If" gate of the text failed, so it now answers NOTHING instead of JUST FALSE (fork F20, name-test sweep of 2026-11-12; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant or a power and the "If" gate of the text failed, so it now answers NOTHING instead of JUST FALSE (fork F20, name-test sweep of 2026-11-12; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
-- s 117(4)
#ASSERT `s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant or a power and the "If" gate of the text failed, so it now answers NOTHING instead of JUST FALSE (fork F21, name-test sweep of 2026-11-12; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant or a power and the "If" gate of the text failed, so it now answers NOTHING instead of JUST FALSE (fork F21, name-test sweep of 2026-11-12; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
